{"title":"Lifting the Exponent Lemma","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Lifting the exponent allows one to calculate the highest power of an integer that divides various numbers given certain information. It is extremely powerful and can sometimes \"blow up\" otherwise challenging problems. \n</p><p>This is a very tuff lemma&#160;:)\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a prime such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/b/49b50c86f55f8da1bade4fe2bafff8d44ef51d8a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\nmid x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/0/350dbef2ab115868f741f51e7020d2b361b6fc03.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p \\nmid y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"36\" height=\"20\" />. LTE comprises of the following identities (where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/d/badd914bca8ef48b2d81b32ef6051cff7047d030.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(Z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"43\" height=\"18\" /> represents the largest power of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that divides <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />):\n</p>\n<ul><li>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is odd:\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/e/82efa92e1f610d9ac1e2e7f940425bd7e0e0b903.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(x^n-y^n)=\\nu_p(x-y)+\\nu_p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"254\" height=\"20\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/e/00e14b620695fabdf6f2f6ec083f95c7b8ec8072.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\mid x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" />.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/4/0a40c2ecf73891c0911b16174624e7bd260d715e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(x^n+y^n)=\\nu_p(x+y)+\\nu_p(n)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"250\" height=\"18\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/938a932db6b2c947be86a292c7f197a3b97e41bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\mid x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/f/6af7099121b05c10ad92ad3c0eb3aecb5e2c1064.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_p(x^n+y^n)=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"126\" height=\"20\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/8/938a932db6b2c947be86a292c7f197a3b97e41bb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p\\mid x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even.</li></ul></li>\n<li>When <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/b/25b803838ba4ded99f094071740c256527784b2e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />:\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/a/caabd115150c9cc0be6f5311b15da2108a0015ed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_2(x^n-y^n)=\\nu_2(x-y)+\\nu_2(x+y)+\\nu_2(n)-1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"376\" height=\"18\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/883a3dad18d58d42da0dae3f624fa3cab4ae599a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\mid x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/0/f90b4188f86db5f85a0b7938231b8535bd379b88.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_2(x^n-y^n)=\\nu_2(x-y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"190\" height=\"20\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/883a3dad18d58d42da0dae3f624fa3cab4ae599a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\mid x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd.</li>\n<li>Corollaries:\n<ul><li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/1/951d031cc4ab67742d0640cffc1d84c6ac12519e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_2(x^n-y^n)=\\nu_2(x-y)+\\nu_2(n),$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"255\" height=\"18\" /> if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/b/33bcffd4f0b1331e579579e89aa041825564edb8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4\\mid x-y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" />.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/f/68f0c58afad79c982fbb81b3194e154271b25d9b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_2(x^n+y^n)=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"123\" height=\"18\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/16568010bf704c103116e699d39a1d15844f7156.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\mid x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is even.</li>\n<li><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/5/3b5f3cd06d16897819ae175179e3c22ea24d7d66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\nu_2(x^n+y^n)=\\nu_2(x+y)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"190\" height=\"20\" />, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/5/16568010bf704c103116e699d39a1d15844f7156.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2\\mid x+y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"68\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is odd.</li></ul></li></ul></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"External_Links\">External Links</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Lifting_the_Exponent_Lemma&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: External Links\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"//arxiv.org/abs/1810.11456\">[1]</a></li>\n<li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external autonumber\" href=\"//services.artofproblemsolving.com/download.php?id=YXR0YWNobWVudHMvYy82LzdjNTI1OGIyMmNjYmZkZGY4MDhhY2ViZTc3MGE1NDRmMzFhMTEzLnBkZg==&amp;rn=TGlmdGluZyBUaGUgRXhwb25lbnQgTGVtbWEgLSBBbWlyIEhvc3NlaW4gUGFydmFyZGkgLSBWZXJzaW9uIDMucGRm\">[2]</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Lifting_the_Exponent_Lemma&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018084402\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.027 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 159/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 319/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument si